# Cloudflare rewrites, evaluated top to bottom (first match wins).
#
# SPA fallback for TanStack Router's client-side routes (e.g. deep-linking to
# /leads/103, which has no file in the static build).
/*  /index.html  200

# NOTE: there is deliberately no `/api/*` proxy rule here.
#
# A `/api/*  https://api.financecrm.com/api/:splat  200` line looks right —
# it is how Netlify proxies to an external origin — but Cloudflare does not
# support it. A 200 rewrite may only target a path inside this project, so the
# rule is silently ignored and the `/*` fallback below it answers instead:
# every /api/* request returns index.html as `text/html` with status 200, and
# a POST returns 405. Verified against the deployed site.
#
# The app therefore calls the API by absolute URL instead, via
# VITE_API_BASE_URL baked in at build time (see src/lib/api.ts). That is
# cross-origin, which is fine on both counts that matter: the API allow-lists
# this origin, and the CRM shares the API's registrable domain so the
# SameSite=lax/strict auth cookies are still treated as same-site.
#
# If you ever want a true same-origin proxy, it takes a real Worker script
# that fetch()es the API — not a rewrite rule.
